// Title: New File Association Using Exefile
// Sigma ID: 44a22d59-b175-4f13-8c16-cbaef5b581ff
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Andreas Hunkeler (@Karneades)
// Date: 2021-11-19 | Modified: 2023-08-17
// ATT&CK: stealth
// Description: Detects the abuse of the exefile handler in new file association. Used for bypass of security
//   products.
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://twitter.com/mrd0x/status/1461041276514623491
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/registry/registry_set/registry_set_file_association_exefile.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceRegistryEvents
| where RegistryKey contains "Classes\\." and RegistryValueData =~ "exefile"
